OK, "Li'l Bow Wow" is just an ordinary kid in school, with an ordinary
life, and ordinary friends.  He lives with his single mom, who is just
trying to raise her kid right, but doesn't time to date, because she has
to balance time with her career with raising her kid.  The kid and his
friends hang out, and do "boy" stuff and have fun all the time, but
there's this little hint that he's special or different from the rest.
There's also this girl at school who he likes, but she doesn't notice
him.

He wants to help his mom out in any way he can, so he writes an essay to
win some contest to become president (???), and much to his surprise, he
wins the contest, and gets to go to the White House. 

Some stuffy White House assistant guy, (who will, no doubt, become the
comic foil for Li'l Bow Wow), shows up at the door and announces the
ballyhoo, which, upon hearing, the mom faints.  Now, he and his mom are
suddenly being mollycoddled around by the White House staff, and paraded
all over in a limousine.  Then, we are treated to a big montage, (to the
tune of some hip hop song), of Bow Wow running all over the White House
wreaking havoc. 

Well, Bow Wow uses his White House "hookup" to get a hold of the girl at
school who never noticed him before.  Now she gets to spend the day with
him, parading through Washington DC on some horse-and-buggy ride, or
something.  She falls for him later that night during the fireworks
display, which he has his White House people set up for him. 

In a subplot story, there's some congressman who opposes some issue that
the President is proposing, and the kid has to go on television and
debate him.  In a great comic scene, the stuffy White House assistant
guy tries to teach him how to act proper for the cameras, and he, in
turn, teaches the stuffy White House guy how to dance. 

The kid goes on television to debate the congressman, and the kid says
something funny or cute, and wins the heart of America.  The congressman
leaves with this "You've won, but it's not over yet" look on his face.
Suddenly, the kid is a hero to all kids everywhere, but his close
friends soon find that he has betrayed them for the fanfare of being
President.  After the big debate, the mom is introduced to the opposing
congress guy and there is a little hint of attraction. 

The congressman tries to romance the mom, but she's still got this, "I
can't get into a relationship, I've got to raise my kid," feeling.  But
he lays a kiss on her, and she instantly changes her tune. 

Some other shit happens, and there's a bunch of funny shit and stuff,
and finally, Li'l Bow Wow realizes that the presidency has gone to his
head, and he has betrayed his friends, who have stuck by him all his
life, and he denounces his position to return to being a kid.  The mom
and the congressman hook up, (of course) and at the end, they move in
with him, and the stuffy White House guy quits his job to be their
butler or some stupid shit.  The end.  (Roll credits, over Li'l Bow
Wow's soon-to-be new hit rap song). 

Well, that's my prediction.  What do you think?  Hmm???  I'll bet you
all five thousand dollars that I am correct. 

